  "paper": {
    "doi": "10.1108/compel-11-2024-0462",
    "full_text": "CREATOR_Machine_Data_2024-11-04.pdf included in fixed release, §6.2.3, Table 6 / Table 8, Appendix B Fig. 19. Downscaled input profiles drive a torque-controlled test PMSM and speed-controlled load machine. Source maximum torque is 0.15 Nm, maximum speed 7050 rpm, maximum DC-link 326 V, maximum current 0.3 Arms."
  },
  "analysis": "Six separate cases combine three driving cycles and two scaled vehicle models. In each case timestamp equality across all four CSVs and 0.5 s grid were verified. Torque and speed CSVs are model-derived inputs; power CSVs are experimental electrical input and mechanical output. MAT copies of the same exports were excluded. The small-profile files have headers; the mid-profile files are headerless. Tested cycle torque magnitudes against the tabled maximum. The speed count is strict equality to the published max, not proximity; e.g. rounded input profiles include values of 7050.1 or 7050.2 rpm.",
  "no_load": "Three separate tests from the no-load README recorded torque during a decreasing speed sweep with two minutes between readings. Rotor outside stator for the first two measurements; rotor inside for the third. Values are reported in Nm, only one recorded torque per speed. Warmup and date differ; cannot identify sensor bias from these records alone.",
  "limits": "Cycle traces include no independently measured iq/id, before/after limit command, DC voltage or shaft torque trace. Speed and torque profiles were both derived from the scaled vehicle models. Same-time power and speed/torque input fields do not validate tracking or active limiting. The six cases reuse one machine. The no-load torque measurements have a distinct acquisition protocol and are not cycle tracking feedback.",
  "reproduce": "Python 3.11+ standard library: python derive_creator_bench.py PM_synchronous_motor.zip OUTPUT_DIR (existing directory)."
}
